Chapter: RocRecRecordField
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Ported from roc-lang/roc, src/eval/test/eval_recursive_data_tests.zig,
 "inspect: recursive nominal deeply nested record recursion":

     Type := [Leaf(Str), Node({ value: Str, child: Type })]
     leaf = Type.Leaf("deep")
     level1 = Type.Node({ value: "level1", child: leaf })
     level2 = Type.Node({ value: "level2", child: level1 })
     main = Type.Node({ value: "level3", child: level2 })

 The recursion passes through a RECORD held by a variant. Codex has no
 anonymous record, so the payload is a named one, `Level`, and the two types
 refer to each other. The port prints the chain of values root first and the
 depth, 3, instead of Roc's inspect form.

Section: Types

  Level = record {
   value : Text,
   child : Ty
  }

  Ty =
   | Leaf (Text)
   | Node (Level)

Section: Functions

  chain : Ty -> Text
  chain (t) =
   when t
    is Leaf (s) -> s
    is Node (lv) -> lv.value & "/" & chain (lv.child)

  depth-of : Ty -> Integer
  depth-of (t) =
   when t
    is Leaf (s) -> 0
    is Node (lv) -> 1 + depth-of (lv.child)

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
   let leaf = Leaf "deep"
   in let level1 = Node (Level { value = "level1", child = leaf })
   in let level2 = Node (Level { value = "level2", child = level1 })
   in let level3 = Node (Level { value = "level3", child = level2 })
   in act
    print-line-uni (chain level3)
    print-line-uni (show (depth-of level3))
   end
  end
